---
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="How Veyro collects, uses, shares and protects personal data on its website and fleet telematics platform." path="/privacy/">
  <p>{site.legalName} ("Veyro", "we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal data we collect, why we collect it and the choices you have. It applies to this website and to the Veyro platform, apps and devices ("Services").</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>For data collected through this website, Veyro is the data controller (data fiduciary). For fleet data that our customers collect using the Services, the customer is the controller and Veyro acts as a processor on the customer's instructions.</p>
  <h2>Data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you give us:</strong> name, company, email, phone number and message content when you request a demo or contact us.</li>
    <li><strong>Website usage data:</strong> pages visited, approximate location derived from IP address, device and browser type.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform data (processed for customers):</strong> vehicle location, trip and sensor data, driver identifiers, driving events and, where enabled, video footage.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How we use data</h2>
  <ul><li>To respond to enquiries and provide demos and quotes.</li><li>To provide, secure and improve the Services.</li><li>To send service communications and, with your consent where required, marketing communications.</li><li>To comply with legal obligations.</li></ul>
  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>We process personal data on the basis of consent, performance of a contract, legitimate interests and legal obligation, as applicable under laws including India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act and the EU and UK GDPR.</p>
  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell personal data. We share it only with service providers who process it for us under contract (for example, cloud hosting, email delivery and, if you accept analytics cookies, Google Analytics), with authorities where required by law and in connection with a business transfer.</p>
  <h2>International transfers and retention</h2>
  <p>Data may be processed in countries other than your own with appropriate safeguards. We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes described or as required by law.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or port your data, to withdraw consent, to object to processing and to lodge a complaint with a data protection authority. To exercise your rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We apply technical and organisational measures to protect personal data. See our <a href="/platform/security/">security page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy and will post the revised version here. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, {site.address.street}, {site.address.city}, {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}, {site.address.countryName}.</p>
</Legal>
